## My answer to the prompt

If you mean **`UAudioCapture`**, you can create it directly as a UObject—no `UAudioCaptureComponent` is needed.

One important limitation: **GameMode only exists on the server.** This captures the microphone on the standalone/listen-server machine, not remote players’ microphones. Dedicated servers should skip microphone capture.

Enable the **Audio Capture** plugin and add `"AudioCapture"` to your game module’s dependencies in `YourGame.Build.cs`.

### MyGameMode.h

Replace `YOURGAME_API` with your project’s API macro.

```cpp
#pragma once

#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "GameFramework/GameModeBase.h"
#include "MyGameMode.generated.h"

class UAudioCapture;

UCLASS()
class YOURGAME_API AMyGameMode : public AGameModeBase
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

protected:
    virtual void BeginPlay() override;
    virtual void EndPlay(
        const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason) override;

private:
    UPROPERTY(Transient)
    TObjectPtr<UAudioCapture> Microphone = nullptr;
};
```

### MyGameMode.cpp

```cpp
#include "MyGameMode.h"
#include "AudioCapture.h"

void AMyGameMode::BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();

    if (GetNetMode() == NM_DedicatedServer)
    {
        return;
    }

    Microphone = NewObject<UAudioCapture>(this);

    if (!Microphone || !Microphone->OpenDefaultAudioStream())
    {
        UE_LOG(LogTemp, Error,
            TEXT("Could not open microphone. Check device and permissions."));
        return;
    }

    Microphone->StartCapturingAudio();

    UE_LOG(LogTemp, Log, TEXT("Microphone capturing: %s"),
        Microphone->IsCapturingAudio() ? TEXT("yes") : TEXT("no"));
}

void AMyGameMode::EndPlay(
    const EEndPlayReason::Type EndPlayReason)
{
    if (Microphone && Microphone->IsCapturingAudio())
    {
        Microphone->StopCapturingAudio();
    }

    // Underlying resources are cleaned up when the UObject is destroyed.
    Microphone = nullptr;

    Super::EndPlay(EndPlayReason);
}
```

